{# The GATE — the product's SECOND chrome, and the peer of `shell` rather than a
   variant of it (BB-415 D6). It frames everything that stands BEFORE the
   product: a surface that is, by definition, outside every workspace.

   WHY IT IS NOT `shell`. The rail is workspace-ambient, and
   its workspace links (`WorkspaceMenuLink`) are denied on a route that
   carries no workspace — so `shell` here would render a navigation with no
   reachable entry, which reads as a defect rather than as a state. It shares no
   slot with `shell` either: that one is a full-viewport flex layout with
   sidebar/header/content/footer/overlay, this one is a brand band beside a form.

   THE BAND, AND NO NAVIGATION. A flat butter field carries the product mark
   and the slogan as one group, centred in its height, over a small production
   line at its foot; the page's own title, description and
   content stand beside it. A gate offers the one thing the page is for and no
   link out, because a link into a workspace the reader may not be in is
   exactly the wrong guess `BbWorkspaceAccessCheck` answers with a 404.

   BUTTER IN BOTH MODES, WITH RYE INK. `scheme-light` keeps the mark's own
   dark-mode rule (its wordmark turns light) from firing on the light band.
   The slogan is plain text: the page's title is its single `h1`.

   ONE FRAMED SPLIT FROM `lg`. Band and form share one rounded frame of about
   1100×640px centred on the page, so the butter stays a field beside the form
   rather than half the screen. Below `lg` the frame dissolves: the band runs
   full width on top and the form follows.

   NOT A SCROLL CONTAINER. `min-h-screen` and the frame's `min-h` let a long
   list grow the page rather than clip itself, which keeps a chooser with
   twenty workspaces readable. #}
<div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass(['gate', 'min-h-screen', 'flex', 'lg:items-center', 'lg:justify-center', 'lg:p-section', 'bg-app', 'text-text']) }}>
  <div class="gate__frame w-full flex flex-col lg:flex-row lg:max-w-[1100px] lg:min-h-[640px] lg:overflow-hidden lg:rounded-md lg:border lg:border-border">
    <aside class="gate__band scheme-light flex flex-col gap-section p-gutter lg:p-section min-h-[220px] lg:basis-[46%] lg:shrink-0 bg-gate-band text-gate-band-ink">
      <div class="flex-1 flex flex-col justify-center gap-section">
        <div class="min-w-0">{% block mark %}{% if mark %}{{ mark }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}</div>
        {# SDC does not apply schema defaults at render time. #}
        <p class="m-0 font-display text-gate-headline text-balance">{{ claim|default("Knead it. Ship it."|t) }}</p>
      </div>
      {# The line: tickets glide along a dashed belt. Decoration only; with
         reduced motion the tickets stand still on it. SMIL needs no CSS of
         its own, and an animation cannot be paused from CSS, so the moving
         and the still row are two groups and the media query picks one. #}
      <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 440 36" class="gate__line block w-full h-auto overflow-hidden" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
        <defs>
          <g id="gate-ticket">
            <rect x="0" y="4" width="34" height="22" rx="3" class="fill-gate-band"/>
            <path d="M7 12h20M7 18h12" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </g>
        </defs>
        <path d="M0 31H440" stroke-dasharray="4 5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <g class="motion-reduce:hidden">
          {% for begin in ['0s', '-3s', '-6s'] %}
            <use href="#gate-ticket"><animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="translate" from="-40 0" to="440 0" dur="9s" begin="{{ begin }}" repeatCount="indefinite"/></use>
          {% endfor %}
        </g>
        <g class="hidden motion-reduce:inline">
          <use href="#gate-ticket" x="60"/>
          <use href="#gate-ticket" x="200"/>
          <use href="#gate-ticket" x="340"/>
        </g>
      </svg>
    </aside>
    <main class="gate__main flex-1 flex items-start lg:items-center justify-center p-gutter lg:p-section bg-app lg:bg-surface">
      <div class="w-full max-w-[420px] flex flex-col gap-group">
        {% if title %}
          <h1 class="gate__title m-0 text-section-title">{{ title }}</h1>
        {% endif %}
        {% if description %}
          <p class="gate__description m-0 text-meta text-text-faint max-w-[40ch]">{{ description }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        <div class="gate__content min-w-0">{% block content %}{% if content %}{{ content }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}</div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</div>
